  "body": "Projects like https://github.com/johnmichel/Library-Detector-for-Chrome try to detect library usage on a page for analytics. As modules, WeakMap and eventually private stage become more popular, many libraries won't leave any signatures that can be detected on a page.\r\n\r\nIf they want to be countable, they'd have to explicitly leave a fingerprint, like say `window.usesLodash = true`. At that point, it might make sense to offer an explicit API for this.\r\n\r\n`console` could provide a simple API, like `reportLibrary(name, version)` that can be queried by other tools or sent to ReportingObservers. This call would be unambiguous and survive bundling, minification, etc.",
